                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dreadfully; awfully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec95b0ba-8cd5-4817-9ad3-ce6e57887998",
                                                "sense_id": "95a77d17-8b04-326e-990f-5047075a9225",
                                                "text": "I am now at liberty to confess, that much which I have heard objected to my late friend’s writings was well-founded. Crude they are, I grant you—a sort of unlicked, incondite things—villainously pranked in an affected array of antique modes and phrases."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eee9bb8b-9504-4eda-87cc-37ef44398701",
                                                "sense_id": "95a77d17-8b04-326e-990f-5047075a9225",
                                                "text": "“You're singing villainously out of tune, Kurrell,” said the Major, truthfully. “Pass me that banjo.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
